<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      ScreenCapture entry removed entirely - real root cause of the
      persistent "the key 'Authorization or Allowed' has an invalid
      value" Fleet failure finally found (confirmed via web search, not
      guessed): macOS 26 (Tahoe, what this Mac runs - see the SDK version
      in mac/Installer/build-pkg.sh's build output) restricts ScreenCapture
      PPPC entries to Authorization: Deny or
      AllowStandardUserToSetSystemService only - Allow is rejected
      outright. Not a UUID-caching issue (ruled out: a genuinely fresh
      PayloadUUID failed identically), not a content bug (CodeRequirement
      confirmed byte-for-byte correct via `codesign -d -r-`) - this is a
      real Apple platform restriction that didn't exist, or wasn't
      enforced, when this profile was first written and confirmed working
      during Phase 2.

      Real, considered tradeoff, not a default: AllowStandardUserToSet
      SystemService needs a live interactive click, reintroducing the
      exact problem this profile originally existed to solve for a
      headless launchd-started agent (see mac/README.md's Phase 2 row -
      "every prior grant... went through some form of live
      user-interaction context, which a plain launchd bootstrap never
      has"). Deny defeats the point entirely. So there is currently no
      way to silently, automatically grant Screen Recording to a headless
      agent via MDM on this macOS version - removing the entry rather
      than picking either broken option.

      Real consequence, confirmed and accepted (not silently absorbed):
      this Mac's existing Screen Recording grant (already in its TCC
      database from earlier testing) is untouched by this change and
      keeps working - reboots, sleep/wake, and ordinary agent restarts
      have already been confirmed live not to reset it (see
      mac/README.md's Phase 2 row, the real cold-reboot test). But a
      *future* fresh install, a TCC reset, or migrating to a different
      Mac would need ONE manual interactive click (launch the agent
      once at a real login session, or grant via System Settings
      directly) before capture would work - no longer something MDM can
      restore unattended. Until that click happens, the agent fails
      closed rather than silently running uncovered (per this project's
      established fail-closed design - see FrameProcessor.swift's and
      HeartbeatMonitor's own doc comments), so the exposure window is a
      locked screen requiring setup, not unblocked content.
    -->
    <key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
    <string>ContentGuard PPPC</string>
    <key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
    <string>com.contentguard.pppc</string>
    <key>PayloadType</key>
    <string>Configuration</string>
    <key>PayloadUUID</key>
    <string>B93AE7BB-B220-4DB4-AB78-F0B1DA17B6D2</string>
    <key>PayloadVersion</key>
    <integer>3</integer>
    <key>PayloadScope</key>
    <string>System</string>
    <key>PayloadRemovalDisallowed</key>
    <true/>
    <key>PayloadContent</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>PayloadType</key>
            <string>com.apple.TCC.configuration-profile-policy</string>
            <key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
            <string>com.contentguard.pppc.payload</string>
            <key>PayloadUUID</key>
            <string>84261996-479A-4C16-B14D-50DBE96350D4</string>
            <key>PayloadVersion</key>
            <integer>3</integer>
            <key>Services</key>
            <dict>
                <key>Accessibility</key>
                <array>
                    <dict>
                        <key>Identifier</key>
                        <string>com.contentguard.agent</string>
                        <key>IdentifierType</key>
                        <string>bundleID</string>
                        <key>CodeRequirement</key>
                        <string>identifier "com.contentguard.agent" and certificate root = H"cda6539309367d134e61fb248ba54c7e1386268e"</string>
                        <key>Authorization</key>
                        <string>Allow</string>
                    </dict>
                </array>
            </dict>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
